# ---- credentials. Never commit, never let a glob catch them.
.env
.env.*
*.key
secrets/
# ...but `.env.*` also matched `.env.example`, which is documentation RUN.md tells the reader to
# consult and which holds an EMPTY key value. Re-included by exact name: a judge cloning this
# repo must be able to see which variables exist without being handed a secret.
!.env.example

# ---- dataset. CC BY-SA 4.0: cite it, do not redistribute it.
# Only code, splits, manifests and hashes belong in the repo.
KuaiRand-Pure/
# also match a SYMLINK to the dataset. `KuaiRand-Pure/` matches a directory; a symlink is
# not one, so a local convenience link would otherwise be a tracked file.
KuaiRand-Pure
*.tar.gz
data/
*.csv

# ---- run artifacts
# `runs/*` rather than `runs/` so the ledgers can be re-included: git cannot
# re-include anything under a directory that was itself excluded.
runs/*
!runs/ledgers/
# The signed ledger IS a graded deliverable ("Run & Iteration Logs"), so it must
# be in the repo. Predictions and models must not be -- they are large and
# regenerable.
runs/ledgers/*.npz
# The content-addressed artifact store holds the EXACT SOURCE the agent wrote for every
# candidate -- the "code diff applied" the run-log requirement asks for, and the only way a
# reader can check the trees this README cites by hash (the rejected BPR implementation, the
# promoted cosine-decay edit). 6 MB of text, so it travels. Predictions and fitted models stay
# excluded; those are large and regenerable.
!runs/artifacts/
experiments/*_out.txt
experiments/sweep_out.txt
*.npz
*.npy
*.pt
*.ckpt

# ---- but the SUBMITTED artifacts must be in the repository.
# `*.csv` (dataset redistribution) and `*.npy` (large, regenerable) are excluded above, and
# that silently excluded the graded prediction file and the validation scores the scorer
# signed -- so a judge cloning this repo could read a manifest full of hashes with nothing
# to check them against. Re-included explicitly, by exact path, not by loosening the globs.
# Test fixtures are SOURCE, not data. The portable-recommender fixture is a 20-row
# synthetic CSV that four suites load; `*.csv` above silently excluded it, so a fresh clone
# would fail those tests with a missing-file error rather than a useful one.
!tests/fixtures/**/*.csv

!submission_compliant/submission_test.csv
!submission_compliant/valid_scores.npy
!submission_research/submission_test.csv
!submission_research/valid_scores.npy
!submission_official/submission_test.csv
!submission_official/valid_scores.npy

# ---- python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
